menu "HAL power"

    config HAL_POWER_BATTERY_MONITOR
        bool "Monitor the battery voltage"
        default n
        help
            Enable only on a board that has the battery voltage divider wired
            to the sense pin below. When enabled, the application starts the
            monitor, shows the low battery pattern, and puts the device into
            deep sleep at a critical level. Only a reset wakes it again.

            Leave this off on a board without the divider. The sense pin then
            floats, and a reading between the absent-battery and the critical
            threshold would put the device to sleep after every boot.

    config HAL_POWER_ADC_CHANNEL
        int "Battery sense ADC1 channel"
        range 0 9
        default 0
        help
            ADC1 channel that reads the battery through a 1:2 voltage divider.
            On the ESP32-S3, ADC1 channel N is GPIO N+1, so the default 0 is
            GPIO1.

endmenu
